     147You are in what was once a lush garden, but over the years, with
     147no one to tend it, it has become a botanical nightmare of fungi,
     147mold, and moss.
     148This is the Sorcerer's Lair.  The walls are covered with exotic runes
     148written in strange, indecipherable scripts;  the only readable phrase
     148reads "NOSIDE SAMOHT".  Strange shadows flit about on the walls, but
     148there is nothing visible to cast them.  Iridescent blue light drips
     148from a stalactite far above, falls towards the floor, and evaporates
     148before touching the ground.  A deep resonant chanting sound vibrates
     148from deep in the ground beneath your feet, and a whispering sound
     148composed of the echoes of long-forgotten spells and cantrips seeps
     148from the walls and fills the air.  Passages exit to the east and west.
     149You are standing on the brink of what appears to be a bottomless pit
     149plunging down into the bowels of the earth.  Ledges run around the
     149pit to the east and west, and a passage leads back to the north.
