     206All is silent.
     207The stream gurgles placidly.
     208The bird's singing is quite melodious.
     209The snake is hissing threateningly.
     210The dragon isn't saying anything (which isn't particularly
     210surprising, seeing that he's dead).
     211The dwarf mutters something in dwarvish.
     212One of the dwarves mutters something in dwarvish.
     213As you enter the passage, you are forced to brush up against
     213some of the green slime.  Instantly it flows down and covers your
     213body, and rapidly digests away all of your flesh.
     214The slime filling the passage to the south blackens and shrivels
     214away into nothingness.
     215The vial explodes into splinters and disintegrates, releasing an
     215oily liquid which rapidly sublimes into a large mushroom-shaped cloud
     215of pale puce vapor smelling like sequoia sap and ozone.
     216The vial explodes into splinters and disintegrates, releasing an
     216oily liquid which rapidly sublimes into a large mushroom-shaped cloud
     216of bright green vapor smelling like pine needles and sea water.
     217The vial explodes into splinters and disintegrates, releasing an
     217oily liquid which rapidly sublimes into a large mushroom-shaped cloud
     217of thick yellow vapor smelling like cheddar cheese and bananas.
     218The vial explodes into splinters and disintegrates, releasing an
     218oily liquid which rapidly sublimes into a large mushroom-shaped cloud
     218of choking green vapor smelling like chlorine and apples.
     219The slime isn't saying anything, just twitching.
     220A strange malaise suddenly afflicts you.  You shiver with chill,
     220and your muscles seem to turn to putty; everything around you
     220becomes grey and unreal. The fit quickly passes, and you find that
     220your body has degenerated back to what it was like before you ate
     220the mushroom.
     221As you swallow the mushroom your mouth becomes numb, and everything
     221seems to swirl around you. The effect quickly passes, and you find
     221that your muscles have bulged unbelievably.
     222The sword halts in mid-air, twirls like a dervish, and chants several
     222bars of "Dies Ire" in a rough tenor voice. It then begins to spin
     222like a rip-saw blade and flies directly at the ogre, who attempts to
     222catch it without success; it strikes him full on the chest. There is
     222a brilliant flash of light, a deafening roar and a cloud of oily grey
     222smoke; when the smoke clears (and your eyes begin working properly
     222again) you see that the ogre has vanished. The sword is lying on the
     222ground, sparking and flaming. Before your eyes it softens and melts,
     222writhes as if in pain, and shrinks rapidly until all that is left is
     222a small silvery ring which cools rapidly.
     223The sword is firmly embedded in the stone, and you aren't strong
     223enough to pull it out.
     224As you attempt to pass the ogre, he grabs you by the scruff of the
     224neck, lifts you up easily, and effortlessly rips your head off.
     225Your axe glows bright orange and fades into nothingness.
     226Your sword jumps into the air, chants several bars of the
     226"Volga Boatman", shoots off several fitful blue sparks, and
     226disintegrates.
     227There is a sharp whistling sound from nowhere. The dwarf shudders
     227and turns into a moth, which then flies away.
     228A clear, liquid chime sounds in midair. A large, four-clawed hand
     228reaches out of the ground, grabs the dwarf, and pulls it down into
     228nothingness.
     229There is a sharp sizzling sound. The dwarf explodes into flame
     229and vanishes.
     230A clear, liquid chime sounds in midair. A long green tentacle
     230covered with sucker disks reaches out from nowhere, grabs the
     230dwarves, and pulls them back to wherever it came from.
     231There is a sharp sizzling sound. The dwarves are engulfed in
     231a wave of fire that appears from nowhere, and are completely
     231incinerated; the flames then vanish into nothingness again.
     232There is a sharp whistling sound from nowhere. The dwarves stiffen,
     232shudder, and melt down into a large puddle of soggy goo that quickly
     232soaks into the ground and vanishes.
     233A clear, liquid chime sounds in midair. A large, four-clawed foot
     233appears in midair and stomps violently downward, missing the dwarf
     233but thoroughly squashing you.
     234There is a sharp sizzling sound. A ball of fire roars out of
     234nowhere, misses the dwarf, bounces off of a wall, and incinerates
     234you.
     235There is a sharp crackling sound from the air above you. The dwarf
     235shudders and turns into a sabre-toothed tiger, which attacks and
     235kills you in short order.
     236A clear, liquid chime sounds in midair. A large and very toothy
     236mouth appears in midair and chomps ferociously. The dwarves
     236manage to evade it, but it bites you in half.
     237There is a sharp sizzling sound. A ball of fire appears from
     237nowhere, misses the dwarves, bounces off of the ground, and
     237explodes violently, incinerating you.
     238There is a sharp crackling sound from the air above you.
     238The dwarves stiffen, fall to the ground, and melt into a
     238large puddle of soggy goo. The goo twitches a few times
     238and then flows at you with incredible speed; it attacks
     238and strangles you with little difficulty.
     239>splurch!<
     239Oh, no! You've turned yourself into a jellyfish, and fallen to the
     239ground and been splattered far and wide! Well, that certainly
     239wasn't very smart!!! You were warned not to use that word near
     239water!
     240The ground begins to shudder ominously, and the very cave walls
     240around you begin to creak and groan! A sulphurious stench fills
     240the air!
     240With an incredible lurch, the ground begins to dance and ripple
     240as though it were liquid! You are thrown off of your feet and
     240tossed violently up and down! The cave walls begin to crumble
     240and split from the stress!
     240There is a terrible ROAR of rending rock!! The cave ceiling
     240splits, and rocks plunge down and smash your lower body to a
     240gooey paste!!
     240There is a violent blast in the distance! Steam and smoke drift
     240into view through the rents in the walls, and furiously-bubbling
     240red-hot lava flows in and surrounds you. The cave ceiling dis-
     240integrates in an incredible orgy of grinding destruction, and
     240the cave walls fall and are pounded into fine dust.
     240You are lying, badly mangled, on a small rock island in a sea of
     240molten lava. Above you, the sky is faintly visible through a
     240thick pall of smoke and steam. A short distance to the north, the
     240remains of a well-house are sinking slowly into the bubbling ooze.
     240There is a distant, sourceless screech of incredible anguish! With
     240a sharp >poof< and a small puff of orange smoke, a bent and bearded
     240elf appears. He is dressed in working clothes, and has a name-tag
     240marked "Ralph" on his shirt. "You blithering idiot!" he storms.
     240"You were warned quite clearly not to use that word near water!!
     240I hadn't gotten all of the bugs out of it yet, and now your
     240incredible incompetence has totally destroyed Colossal Cave!! Do
     240you have the faintest scintilla of an iota of an understanding of
     240how much work I'm going to have to do to get the cave rebuilt?!?
     240I'll have to go all the way to Peking for another dragon, and
     240I'll have to convince the Goblin's Union to send me another
     240team of gooseberry goblins; I'll have to sub-contract the building
     240of the volcano out to the local totrugs, and worst of all I'll
     240have to go through eight months of paperwork and red tape to
     240file a new Environmental Impact statement!! All because you
     240couldn't follow directions, you purblind and meatbrained
     240moron! I'm rescinding all of your game points and throwing
     240you out! Out! OUT! GET OUT!$!%#&'@%!!%%!"
     241A giant green tentacle covered with sucker disks reaches
     241from the ground with a great slurping noise, grabs you,
     241and pulls you into nothingness.
     242The minotaur's wall silently crumbles, revealing dark
     242passages leading northwest, north, and northeast.
     243You walked right into the minotaur's wall!
     244Adventure 1.2 (462 points)
     245Suddenly and without warning, there appears from within the very
     245cave walls around you a horde of vicious little goblins! Each one
     245stands about eight inches high on a pair of spindly black legs,
     245has a globular, spine-covered body resembling a giant gooseberry,
     245a wide mouth filled with sharp teeth, and a pair of glittering
     245little green eyes! They swarm around you and try to block your
     245way.
     246One of the gooseberry goblins begins to giggle in a high-pitched
     246voice. Another takes up the giggling, then another... Soon all
     246of them are giggling insanely and jumping up and down with glee!
     247The goblins are jumping up and down frantically, and are working
     247themselves into a real slavering frenzy!!
     248With a shrill cry, the gooseberry goblins hurl themselves upon
     248you, tickling you mercilessly. You crush and hurl away several
     248of them, but are soon borne down by the endless attack. The
     248goblins then gleefully rip out your throat, and you sink into
     248unconsciousness.
     249As each of the dragon's teeth strikes the ground, a fully-armed
     249human skeleton springs up from where it struck and leaps to your
     249defense! The skeletal warriors attack the vicious gooseberry
     249goblins and drive them away in screaming panic; they then salute
     249you with their ancient and rusty swords, and fade silently into
     249nothingness.
     250The basilisk stirs grumpily and awakens, peering sleepily about.
     250It spies you, growls, and stares you straight in the eye. Your
     250body is instantly petrified.
     251The basilisk stirs grumpily and awakens, peering sleepily about.
     251It sees its reflection in the metal plate that you are carrying,
     251shudders, and turns into solid granite.
     252The basilisk stirs restlessly and grumbles in its sleep as you
     252pass, but it does not awaken.
     253The little bird attacks the basilisk, and in an astounding flurry
     253succeeds in awakening it. The basilisk glares at the bird, causing
     253the bird to explode into a cloud of fine sand, and then turns and
     253stares balefully at you, turning you into a pillar of fine marble
     253suitable for decorative lawn or garden use.
     254As you pluck the sceptre from the skeleton's bony grasp,
     254it lifts its head and whispers in a forboding tone:
     254"it's not a bug, it's a feature!". It then collapses
     254into a pile of dust which floats away into the still cave
     254air.
     255Having problems?
     256Okay - what you need to do is apply a little philosophy. To wit:
     256there is a question that you need to ask whenever you explore a new
     256room in this cave. In most places, the answer to the question is
     256"yes". In some other places, it's "no" for an obvious reason. Right
     256here, the answer is "no" but the reason isn't so obvious. If you can
     256figure out what the question is, you can get out of here easily. I
     256can tell you this - it's always a vital question if you wish to
     256survive.
     257A faint glow of light is visible through the fog to the east.
     258A glimmer of light is visible through the fog in the west.
     259A glow of light is visible through the fog to the north.
     260A faint shimmer of light is visible to the south.
     261A flickering light is visible through the fog in the northeast.
     262A dim light is visible in the southeast
     263A dim glow of light is visible in the southwest.
     264A dim flickering light is visible through the fog in the northwest.
     265You have set the flask down in the center of the pentagram.
     266The flask's wax seal breaks away easily, and a cloud of dark smoke
     266pours from the mouth of the flask and condenses into the form of a
     266twelve-foot djinn standing in the pentagram. He pushes experimentally
     266at the magical wall of the pentagram (which holds), and nods politely
     266to you. "My thanks, oh mortal," he says in an incredibly deep bass
     266voice. "It has been three thousand years since Solomon sealed me
     266into that bottle, and I am grateful that you have released me. If
     266you will open this pentagram and let me go free, I will give you
     266some advice that you may one day wish to possess."
     267The flask is already open!
     268The flask's wax seal crumbles at your touch. A large cloud of black
     268smoke pours out, solidifying into the form of a twelve-foot Djinn.
     268"At last!" he says in an earth-shaking voice, "I knew that someday
     268someone would release me! I would reward you for this, mortal, but
     268it has been three thousand years since I had a solid meal, and I'm
     268not going to stand here chattering when I could be out eating a six-
     268inch sirloin steak. Farewell." With that, he somewhat rudely explodes
     268back into smoke and drifts quickly out of sight.
     269There's nothing to let out of the pentagram!
     270The pentagram's magical barrier sparks fitfully and goes down.
     270The djinn stretches gratefully and smiles at you. "Again my thanks,"
     270he says, "I will tell you a piece of ancient lore which I learned from
     270my aunt, an afreet of great knowledge. There is another magic word
     270that you might find of use if you should ever find yourself being
     270attacked by those pestiferous dwarves. You should only use it as
     270a last resort, though, since it is a most potent word and is
     270prone to backfire for no obvious reason; also, it should never
     270be used near water or any sharp weapon or the results may be most
     270UNFORTUNATE. THE WORD IS 'phuggg'", whispers the djinn, "AND IT
     270must be pronounced carefully if it is to have the proper effect.
     270Farewell, and good luck!" With that, the djinn-cloud drifts away
     270out of sight.
     271The dragon is breathing heavily, occasionally snorting little puffs
     271of smoke.
     272There is nothing here you can take.
